### Step 3: Architecting the LangGraph FSM (Cognitive Engine)

We are going to define the agent as a Finite State Machine. In Phase 1, the graph is a simple loop (`START -> agent -> END`), but because it extends `MessagesAnnotation`, injecting an MCP "Tools" node in Phase 2 will require changing just one line of routing logic.

Create a new directory and file at **`src/lib/agent/graph.ts`**:

```typescript
import { StateGraph, MessagesAnnotation, MemorySaver } from "@langchain/langgraph";
import { ChatOllama } from "@langchain/ollama";
import { SystemMessage } from "@langchain/core/messages";

// 1. Initialize the Local LLM natively interacting with Ollama
const llm = new ChatOllama({
  model: "qwen2.5-coder:7b", // Must match the model you pulled
  baseUrl: "http://localhost:11434", // Default Ubuntu Ollama port
  temperature: 0.1, // Low temperature is critical for deterministic agent behavior later
});

// 2. Define the Agent Node
async function callModel(state: typeof MessagesAnnotation.State) {
  const { messages } = state;
  
  // Prepend the system prompt dynamically
  const systemPrompt = new SystemMessage(
    "You are a highly capable autonomous AI agent running natively on an Ubuntu system. " +
    "You are currently in Phase 1 of your initialization. Be concise, helpful, and acknowledge your local environment."
  );
  
  // The LLM processes the system prompt + conversation history
  const response = await llm.invoke([systemPrompt, ...messages]);
  
  // Return the new message. LangGraph's reducer automatically appends it to the state.
  return { messages: [response] };
}

// 3. Construct the Finite State Machine (Graph)
const workflow = new StateGraph(MessagesAnnotation)
  .addNode("agent", callModel)
  .addEdge("__start__", "agent")
  .addEdge("agent", "__end__"); // In Phase 2, this edge will conditionally route to the Tool Node

// 4. Initialize Short-Term Memory
// We use MemorySaver for Phase 1. In Phase 4, we will swap this with PostgresSaver/pgvector.
const checkpointer = new MemorySaver();

// Compile into a runnable application
export const agentGraph = workflow.compile({ checkpointer });

```

